          "In addition, separating validation, auditing, and storage into clean interfaces enables seamless integration with cross-cutting aspect-oriented programming (AOP) interceptors. Security frameworks can intercept validate() calls to enforce role-based access control, while telemetry frameworks can intercept saveToStorage() calls to publish distributed tracing spans to OpenTelemetry collectors without cluttering domain logic.",
          "Take a moment to compare how a novice approaches Mastery Assignment: Multi-Interface Auditable Entity versus how a seasoned specialist handles it. A novice looks only at the final output number, whereas a specialist inspects how passport interacts with travel, checks whether getAuditLog remains within expected operating bounds, and verifies the fallback behavior when validate hits an extreme edge case. That habit of checking both the happy path and the boundary condition is what turns textbook knowledge into reliable professional judgment."
